7. Troubleshooting
ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'paddle'
You haven't installed Paddle yet, OR

You switched runtime types after installing.

Fix: run section 2 (CPU) or 3 (GPU), then restart and re-run section 1.

ImportError: libtorch_cuda.so: undefined symbol: ncclCommShrink
Torch was broken by the Paddle GPU install.

Fix: !pip uninstall -y torch torchvision torchaudio, then restart.

RuntimeError: PDX has already been initialized
PaddleX initialized once already in this kernel.

Fix: Runtime → Restart session.

Cannot connect to GPU backend
Colab's free-tier GPU quota is exhausted.

Fix: wait ~12–24 hours, use a different Google account, or upgrade to Colab Pro.

Slow inference (~100s per image)
You're on CPU. GPU does ~15–25s per image.

Confirm with !nvidia-smi. If no GPU, consider section 3 once quota resets.

Model files re-downloading on every restart
PADDLE_PDX_MODEL_SOURCE wasn't set, or was set to a non-Drive path.

Fix: run section 1 to set it to /content/drive/MyDrive/paddlex_models.

git pull fails with local modifications
Colab shouldn't leave local edits, but if it does:

!cd /content/MeterSerial_VLM && git stash && git pull

