Notes
The setup cell is idempotent — safe to run multiple times. If the repo exists, it pulls; if not, it clones. If Drive is mounted, it skips.

The auto-detect backend means you never need to manually change device="gpu" to "cpu". It handles this internally.

Model cache on Drive means the ~230 MB of PaddleOCR models download only once per session type. On CPU session they're a different set than on GPU session — but Drive keeps both.

The whole document is one markdown file — commit it once, reference it forever. Next time you spin up a session, just open the README from the repo and copy the setup cell.
